Sval: about:license and about:buildconfig allow chrome: fonts

Sval draws Firefox's pages in its own typeface through SvalPageStyle, whose
sheets declare Outfit from a chrome: URL. These two pages set a <meta> CSP of
default-src 'none' with no font-src, and a chrome: font is subject to a
page's CSP whichever sheet asks for it (subjectToCSP, nsCSPService.cpp), so
the font is refused. No chrome API changes a document's own CSP, so each
policy gains font-src chrome:.

diff --git a/toolkit/content/buildconfig.html b/toolkit/content/buildconfig.html
index 15d1e9b173..06e9945865 100644
--- a/toolkit/content/buildconfig.html
+++ b/toolkit/content/buildconfig.html
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 #include @TOPOBJDIR@/source-repo.h
 <html>
   <head>
-    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src chrome:; object-src 'none'" />
+    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src chrome:; font-src chrome:; object-src 'none'" />
     <meta charset="UTF-8">
     <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
     <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width; user-scalable=false;">
diff --git a/toolkit/content/license.html b/toolkit/content/license.html
index ef71884220..15ec470df7 100644
--- a/toolkit/content/license.html
+++ b/toolkit/content/license.html
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 
 <html lang="en">
   <head>
-    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src chrome:; img-src chrome:; object-src 'none'">
+    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src chrome:; img-src chrome:; font-src chrome:; object-src 'none'">
     <meta charset="utf-8">
     <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
     <title>Licenses</title>
